# NCDC Conference Management System

Conference management platform for the National Curriculum Development Centre (NCDC), Uganda.

## Before Writing Code

- Read Next.js docs in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` — this project uses Next.js 16 with breaking changes.
- Follow existing patterns in the codebase before introducing new abstractions.
- Keep changes focused; do not refactor unrelated code.

## Theme & Visual Design

**Always use the shared theme.** Do not introduce ad-hoc colors, fonts, or icon libraries.

| Resource | Location |
|----------|----------|
| CSS variables & Tailwind tokens | `src/theme/theme.css` |
| JS tokens (charts, PDFs, etc.) | `src/theme/tokens.js` |
| UI components | `src/components/ui/` |
| Theme preview | `/theme` route |

### Color Palette (NCDC green)

- **Primary**: `#008e51` — buttons, links, active states, key accents
- **Primary dark**: `#006941` — hover/pressed states
- **Primary light**: `#e8f4ed` — subtle highlights, selected rows
- **Neutrals**: `#313233` text, `#627792` muted text, `#dddfe3` borders
- **Semantic**: success `#15803d`, warning `#b45309`, error `#cf2e2e`, info `#0e2b5c`

Use Tailwind classes: `bg-primary`, `text-primary`, `border-border`, `text-muted-foreground`, etc.

### Design Principles

- Clean, institutional, professional — not flashy or overly decorative
- White/light gray surfaces; green reserved for actions and emphasis
- Subtle borders and shadows; avoid heavy gradients or bright accents
- Consistent `rounded-md` corners (not pill-shaped unless intentional)
- Prefer Geist Sans (`font-sans`) for all UI text

## Icons

- Use **Lucide React** (`lucide-react`) exclusively
- Wrap icons with `<Icon icon={SomeIcon} size="md" />` from `@/components/ui/Icon`
- Sizes: `sm` (16px), `md` (20px), `lg` (24px), `xl` (32px)
- Stroke width: 1.75 (set by Icon wrapper — do not override unless necessary)

## Buttons

Use `<Button>` from `@/components/ui/Button`:

```jsx
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/Button";
import { Plus } from "lucide-react";

<Button variant="primary" icon={Plus}>Register</Button>
<Button variant="secondary">Cancel</Button>
<Button variant="outline">View details</Button>
<Button variant="ghost">Back</Button>
<Button variant="danger">Delete</Button>
```

Variants: `primary` | `secondary` | `ghost` | `outline` | `danger`
Sizes: `sm` | `md` | `lg`

## File Structure

```
src/
  app/           # Next.js App Router pages & layouts
  components/
    ui/          # Reusable themed UI primitives
  lib/           # Utilities (cn, helpers)
  theme/         # Design tokens & CSS variables
```

## Code Conventions

- JavaScript (`.js`/`.jsx`) unless TypeScript is explicitly requested
- Functional React components; colocate related files
- Use `@/` path alias for imports (configured in `jsconfig.json`)
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/cn` for conditional class names
- Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only when needed

## Naming

- Components: PascalCase (`ConferenceCard.jsx`)
- Files/routes: kebab-case for routes, match component name for components
- CSS: Tailwind utility classes; no inline styles unless dynamic values require it

## Accessibility

- Semantic HTML (`button`, `nav`, `main`, `label`)
- Visible focus rings (already styled on Button)
- `aria-label` on icon-only buttons
- Sufficient color contrast — do not lighten primary green for body text

## What Not To Do

- Do not use random hex colors — use theme tokens
- Do not add new UI libraries (MUI, Chakra, etc.) without explicit approval
- Do not use emoji as icons
- Do not enable dark mode unless explicitly requested — theme is light-first
- Do not create commits unless the user asks
